  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nWe've learned that Chromium and WebKit don't load images with whitespace-only `src`. It looks to me that the spec excludes only empty-string `src`, and this turns out to be a Web compat issue for Gecko when an extra `GET` to the document's URL has adverse cookie side effects. Also, it seems that at least WebKit also has a similar rule for `src` on `script`.\n\nThe points in the spec that currently reject empty `src` should be changed to reject empty or whitespace-only `src` when there's a major browser already doing so. (For completeness, it's probably worthwhile to test if the existing checks in browsers operate on HTML whitespace or XML whitespace. I haven't looked.)\n\nGecko bugs:\n* https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2010794\n* https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2016516",
